<p>US President Donald Trump warned on Monday that countries trying to reopen or back away from recently negotiated US trade deals would face substantially higher import duties, after a US Supreme Court ruling struck down his emergency tariff program. Trump cast the decision as shutting down one tariff tool while still leaving him room to escalate through other approaches he described as more forceful. The administration said it will stop collecting the levies the Supreme Court found illegal, leaving businesses and governments waiting for guidance on practical questions like refunds and how existing trade arrangements will work going forward.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mhjw_EYg8fqVsiXkmo_ALDteWPsOfUZnSol8Bd-gk8O6dlCtGAunNh0d0honRuiiZvQ2PUyPSjRY_1uwdyMbay6s-42F9N2qK1HGGcO8AaGe' alt='US President Donald Trump gestures at the White House in Washington, DC, on February 23, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>What the court blocked: The Supreme Court ruled Friday that Trump exceeded his authority by using emergency powers for a sweeping global tariff push tied to his “liberation day” measures.</li><li>Trump’s escalation message: Trump said countries shouldn’t use the ruling to revisit newly agreed terms, and he claimed he could impose tariffs in a “much more powerful and obnoxious way” through other avenues.</li><li>What the EU pause concerns: European Parliament negotiators moved to freeze approval steps for a transatlantic deal aimed at removing tariffs on US industrial goods, citing uncertainty after the ruling.</li><li>Operational fallout: After the US said it will stop collecting the levies found illegal, companies are waiting for details on refunds or adjustments and how import payments will be reconciled.</li></ul><blockquote>Any country that wants to ‘play games’ with the ridiculous supreme court decision, especially those that have ‘Ripped Off’ the US for years, and even decades, will be met with a much higher tariff, and worse, than that which they just recently agreed to - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He said countries that use the Supreme Court decision to revisit recently agreed terms would face “much higher” tariffs, and he suggested he could turn to other tariff tools he sees as more forceful. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yvky5ldk1o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>China commerce ministry: Beijing urged Washington to cancel unilateral tariff measures, saying it is assessing the ruling and repeating that trade wars have no winners. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975335/trump-warns-countries-against-playing-games-with-tariffs'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>European Parliament trade negotiators: EU lawmakers moved to pause approval steps for a transatlantic deal that would remove tariffs on US industrial goods, citing uncertainty after the court ruling. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975335/trump-warns-countries-against-playing-games-with-tariffs'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>UK and EU governments: Officials said they want urgent clarity from Washington on the trade deals struck last summer as the US moves to stop collecting levies the court ruled illegal. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/23/us-stop-collecting-trump-tariffs-supreme-court-dollar-gold-ieepa-refunds'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/donald-trump-higher-tariff-warning-for-countries-wanting-to-play-games-supreme-court-ruling-11127696#publisher=newsstand'>Trump&#x27;s Higher Tariff Warning For Countries Wanting To &quot;Play Games&quot;</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rd1jm8/trump_warns_countries_that_play_games_with_us/'>Trump warns countries that &#x27;play games&#x27; with US trade deals will face higher tariffs</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/any-country-that-wants-to-play-games-donald-trump-warns-of-more-obnoxious-tariffs-as-eu-mulls-pausing-us-trade-deal-13982878.html'>‘Any country that wants to play games…’: Trump warns of ‘more obnoxious’ tariffs as EU mulls pausing US trade deal</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yvky5ldk1o'>Trump threatens countries that &#x27;play games&#x27; with existing trade deals</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/23/us-stop-collecting-trump-tariffs-supreme-court-dollar-gold-ieepa-refunds'>Trump threatens ‘obnoxious’ tariffs as UK and EU seek clarity on trade deals</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975335/trump-warns-countries-against-playing-games-with-tariffs'>Trump warns countries against ‘playing games’ with tariffs</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>